WEBVTT

00:03.960 --> 00:04.640
So quickly.

00:04.640 --> 00:05.680
What is ChatGPT?

00:05.840 --> 00:11.880
It is an AI program that is developed by OpenAI that is trained to understand questions and provide

00:11.880 --> 00:13.280
human like answers.

00:13.400 --> 00:15.280
So what GPT stands for.

00:15.440 --> 00:17.240
The G stands for generative.

00:17.240 --> 00:21.600
So that means the data model can generate a new content new text.

00:21.640 --> 00:23.720
And P stands for pre-trained.

00:23.720 --> 00:27.360
The data model is already trained on huge amounts of data.

00:27.360 --> 00:29.400
And the T stands for transformer.

00:29.440 --> 00:35.520
It is a type of neural network architecture that processes your sentences in the prompts in order to

00:35.520 --> 00:39.360
understand the context behind it very fast and accurate.

00:39.360 --> 00:42.080
And in the other hand, we have the GitHub copilot.

00:42.120 --> 00:47.320
It is developed by the GitHub and as well using the same data models from the OpenAI.

00:47.600 --> 00:50.840
So that means both ChatGPT and Copilot.

00:50.880 --> 00:55.880
Both of them are using the same language model that is developed from OpenAI.

00:56.160 --> 01:01.440
So the GitHub copilot did train on tons of codes that is available in GitHub.

01:01.440 --> 01:06.660
So how it works as you are writing a code in the code editor, like for example, Visual Studio.

01:06.700 --> 01:11.620
It can provide real time suggestions as you are writing and typing your code.

01:11.620 --> 01:17.220
So now if you compare those two ChatGPT and the copilot, we can say that the ChatGPT is a stand alone

01:17.220 --> 01:23.380
application where you can interact with it using a website or an app, where you go and start a conversation

01:23.380 --> 01:29.620
with the AI, where in the other hand, the copilot is directly integrated in your code editor, like

01:29.620 --> 01:31.540
for example, the Visual Studio Code.

01:31.580 --> 01:36.420
This is way better than ChatGPT because you have real time interaction with the AI.

01:36.620 --> 01:40.580
This is a great advantage for the copilot because everything in one place.

01:40.580 --> 01:45.140
So with the copilot you are getting real time assistance during your coding.

01:45.420 --> 01:51.540
So the main purpose of the ChatGPT is to have a conversation with the AI for any topic that you like,

01:51.580 --> 01:58.580
not limited only for software development, but in the other hand, the copilot focuses only on assisting

01:58.580 --> 02:00.100
the software development.

02:00.100 --> 02:05.060
Where you as a developer, as you are writing your code, you are getting autocompletion of the code

02:05.100 --> 02:07.900
or maybe a block of code as a suggestion.

02:07.900 --> 02:11.740
So these are the key differences between ChatGPT and Copilot.
